= Tutorial
Seven steps from an empty file to Bird Watch, a program that counts the
birds at the feeder: a window, a menu, a counter, a timer, the mouse, colour
and keys, sound. Each step's listing is the whole program; type it into
VeraBASIC, the editor, and press Ctrl+R to run it (F1 on a keyword shows its
help page). The steps are in /DOCUMENTS/VeraBASIC Examples too.

Each listing is a program of gate vb_ui (tests/vbasic/ui/bird1.bas to
bird7.bas), played there with the mouse and the keys and compared with the
reference interpreter. The statements are in the chapter The Veranda
extensions (extensions.md).

OPTION INTEGER at the top makes names without a suffix integers: faster, and
what new programs should use.

@{Step 1: A window}
@{Step 2: A menu with About and Quit}
@{Step 3: A counter in the status bar}
@{Step 4: A timer}
@{Step 5: A click handler}
@{Step 6: Colour and keys}
@{Step 7: Sound, and asking before quitting}

= Step 1: A window
A Veranda program draws its own window: WINDOW #1 takes the window's place
and size in cards (8 x 8 pixels: 80 across, 60 down), its title and its
options. CLOSE gives it a close glyph, FRAME a frame, SHADOW a shadow,
STATUS 2 a status band of two card rows at the bottom.

WINDOW USE #1 makes the window's body the place where the drawing goes: from
now on TEXT 16, 20 is 16 pixels right of the body's left edge and 20 down
from its top, and nothing is drawn outside the body.

ON CLOSE #1 CALL DoQuit is the first event: a click on the close glyph calls
the SUB DoQuit. When the main lines end, the program waits for its events;
END in a handler ends it.

  ' Bird Watch, step 1: a window
  OPTION INTEGER
  APP NAME "Bird Watch"
  WINDOW #1, 10, 6, 60, 40, "Bird Watch", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW, STATUS 2
  WINDOW USE #1
  FONT UI
  TEXT 16, 20, "Birds at the feeder"
  ON CLOSE #1 CALL DoQuit

  SUB DoQuit
    END
  END SUB

Run it: VeraBASIC Run opens the window over the desk. Click the cross at the
top right: the program ends.

= Step 2: A menu with About and Quit
MENU "title" starts a menu of the bar; each ITEM "text", Sub after it is an
item that calls a SUB. ITEM "Quit", DoQuit, "Q" also has a shortcut: Ctrl+Q.
MENU SHOW puts the bar up.

The first menu is always named after the program (the Look 2 rule): its APP
NAME. Its About item opens a second window with a close glyph of its own; ON
CLOSE #2 closes it again with WINDOW CLOSE #2, which erases it to the desk.

Note that About ends with WINDOW USE #1: the drawing goes back to the main
window.

  ' Bird Watch, step 2: a menu with About and Quit
  OPTION INTEGER
  APP NAME "Bird Watch"
  WINDOW #1, 10, 6, 60, 40, "Bird Watch", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW, STATUS 2
  WINDOW USE #1
  FONT UI
  TEXT 16, 20, "Birds at the feeder"
  MENU "Bird Watch" : ITEM "About Bird Watch", About
  MENU "File" : ITEM "Quit", DoQuit, "Q"
  MENU SHOW
  ON CLOSE #1 CALL DoQuit
  ON CLOSE #2 CALL CloseAbout

  SUB About
    WINDOW #2, 25, 18, 30, 8, "About", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW
    WINDOW USE #2
    FONT UI
    TEXT 12, 20, "Bird Watch 1.0"
    TEXT 12, 36, "Counts the birds at the feeder."
    WINDOW USE #1
  END SUB

  SUB CloseAbout
    WINDOW CLOSE #2
  END SUB

  SUB DoQuit
    END
  END SUB

Choose Bird Watch > About Bird Watch, close the About window with its cross,
then File > Quit.

= Step 3: A counter in the status bar
A third menu, Birds, counts. count is a global variable: a SUB can read and
change it. ShowCount writes it into the status band with WINDOW STATUS #1,
left$, right$.

ShowCount on a line of its own calls the SUB: a SUB is called by its name,
as a statement.

  ' Bird Watch, step 3: a counter in the status bar
  OPTION INTEGER
  APP NAME "Bird Watch"
  WINDOW #1, 10, 6, 60, 40, "Bird Watch", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW, STATUS 2
  WINDOW USE #1
  FONT UI
  TEXT 16, 20, "Birds at the feeder"
  MENU "Bird Watch" : ITEM "About Bird Watch", About
  MENU "File" : ITEM "Quit", DoQuit, "Q"
  MENU "Birds" : ITEM "Add a bird", AddBird, "B" : ITEM "Start again", Reset
  MENU SHOW
  count = 0
  ShowCount
  ON CLOSE #1 CALL DoQuit
  ON CLOSE #2 CALL CloseAbout

  SUB About
    WINDOW #2, 25, 18, 30, 8, "About", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW
    WINDOW USE #2
    FONT UI
    TEXT 12, 20, "Bird Watch 1.0"
    TEXT 12, 36, "Counts the birds at the feeder."
    WINDOW USE #1
  END SUB

  SUB CloseAbout
    WINDOW CLOSE #2
  END SUB

  SUB AddBird
    count = count + 1
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB Reset
    count = 0
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB ShowCount
    WINDOW STATUS #1, STR$(count) + " birds", ""
  END SUB

  SUB DoQuit
    END
  END SUB

Choose Birds > Add a bird a few times (or press Ctrl+B), then Start again.

= Step 4: A timer
TIMER 1, 60 CALL Tick calls Tick every 60 frames: once a second. Tick shows
the count again, with the time (TIME$) at the right of the status band.
Timers, menus and clicks are all events: each handler runs to its end before
the next starts, so Tick never interrupts AddBird.

  ' Bird Watch, step 4: a timer
  OPTION INTEGER
  APP NAME "Bird Watch"
  WINDOW #1, 10, 6, 60, 40, "Bird Watch", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW, STATUS 2
  WINDOW USE #1
  FONT UI
  TEXT 16, 20, "Birds at the feeder"
  MENU "Bird Watch" : ITEM "About Bird Watch", About
  MENU "File" : ITEM "Quit", DoQuit, "Q"
  MENU "Birds" : ITEM "Add a bird", AddBird, "B" : ITEM "Start again", Reset
  MENU SHOW
  count = 0
  ShowCount
  TIMER 1, 60 CALL Tick
  ON CLOSE #1 CALL DoQuit
  ON CLOSE #2 CALL CloseAbout

  SUB About
    WINDOW #2, 25, 18, 30, 8, "About", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW
    WINDOW USE #2
    FONT UI
    TEXT 12, 20, "Bird Watch 1.0"
    TEXT 12, 36, "Counts the birds at the feeder."
    WINDOW USE #1
  END SUB

  SUB CloseAbout
    WINDOW CLOSE #2
  END SUB

  SUB AddBird
    count = count + 1
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB Reset
    count = 0
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB ShowCount
    WINDOW STATUS #1, STR$(count) + " birds", TIME$
  END SUB

  SUB Tick
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB DoQuit
    END
  END SUB

Watch the clock in the status band while you add birds.

= Step 5: A click handler
ON CLICK CALL Clicked binds the mouse. A click calls the handler twice: once
for the press and once for the release; MOUSEB AND 128 is the release, which
Clicked leaves alone.

HIT(#1, MOUSEX, MOUSEY) says where the click was: 4 is the window's body (1
the title band, 2 the close glyph, 5 the status band, 0 outside). Since
window 1 is in use, MOUSEX and MOUSEY are in its body's coordinates, the
same as the drawing's, so DrawBird MOUSEX, MOUSEY draws a bird where you
clicked: a BOX and two LINEs.

DrawBird(x, y) is a SUB with arguments; its x and y are its own.

  ' Bird Watch, step 5: a click handler
  OPTION INTEGER
  APP NAME "Bird Watch"
  WINDOW #1, 10, 6, 60, 40, "Bird Watch", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW, STATUS 2
  WINDOW USE #1
  FONT UI
  TEXT 16, 20, "Birds at the feeder"
  MENU "Bird Watch" : ITEM "About Bird Watch", About
  MENU "File" : ITEM "Quit", DoQuit, "Q"
  MENU "Birds" : ITEM "Add a bird", AddBird, "B" : ITEM "Start again", Reset
  MENU SHOW
  count = 0
  ShowCount
  TIMER 1, 60 CALL Tick
  ON CLICK CALL Clicked
  ON CLOSE #1 CALL DoQuit
  ON CLOSE #2 CALL CloseAbout

  SUB About
    WINDOW #2, 25, 18, 30, 8, "About", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW
    WINDOW USE #2
    FONT UI
    TEXT 12, 20, "Bird Watch 1.0"
    TEXT 12, 36, "Counts the birds at the feeder."
    WINDOW USE #1
  END SUB

  SUB CloseAbout
    WINDOW CLOSE #2
  END SUB

  SUB Clicked
    IF MOUSEB AND 128 THEN EXIT SUB
    IF HIT(#1, MOUSEX, MOUSEY) <> 4 THEN EXIT SUB
    DrawBird MOUSEX, MOUSEY
    AddBird
  END SUB

  SUB DrawBird(x, y)
    WINDOW USE #1
    BOX x - 3, y - 2, x + 3, y + 2
    LINE x - 8, y - 6, x, y
    LINE x, y, x + 8, y - 6
  END SUB

  SUB AddBird
    count = count + 1
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB Reset
    count = 0
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB ShowCount
    WINDOW STATUS #1, STR$(count) + " birds", TIME$
  END SUB

  SUB Tick
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB DoQuit
    END
  END SUB

Click in the window: a bird for each click, and the counter goes up. Clicks
outside the window's body do nothing.

= Step 6: Colour and keys
The screen has one ink colour, but each 8 x 8 card has a paper colour of its
own: PAPER column, row, width, height, colour paints cards. A hill (GREEN)
under a sky (SKY2), in the colours of Veranda's look. CARDS writes in the
ROM's 8 x 8 font on the card grid.

ON KEY CALL Typed binds the keyboard: in Typed, KEY$ is the key. b draws a
bird in a row, c starts again, which now also clears the birds with a BOX in
pattern 0 (the paper) and back to pattern 1 (ink).

  ' Bird Watch, step 6: colour and keys
  OPTION INTEGER
  APP NAME "Bird Watch"
  WINDOW #1, 10, 6, 60, 40, "Bird Watch", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW, STATUS 2
  WINDOW USE #1
  FONT UI
  TEXT 16, 20, "Birds at the feeder"
  PAPER 0, 28, 60, 8, GREEN
  PAPER 0, 3, 60, 25, SKY2
  CARDS 40, 1, "Keys: B, C"
  ON KEY CALL Typed
  MENU "Bird Watch" : ITEM "About Bird Watch", About
  MENU "File" : ITEM "Quit", DoQuit, "Q"
  MENU "Birds" : ITEM "Add a bird", AddBird, "B" : ITEM "Start again", Reset
  MENU SHOW
  count = 0
  ShowCount
  TIMER 1, 60 CALL Tick
  ON CLICK CALL Clicked
  ON CLOSE #1 CALL DoQuit
  ON CLOSE #2 CALL CloseAbout

  SUB About
    WINDOW #2, 25, 18, 30, 8, "About", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW
    WINDOW USE #2
    FONT UI
    TEXT 12, 20, "Bird Watch 1.0"
    TEXT 12, 36, "Counts the birds at the feeder."
    WINDOW USE #1
  END SUB

  SUB CloseAbout
    WINDOW CLOSE #2
  END SUB

  SUB Clicked
    IF MOUSEB AND 128 THEN EXIT SUB
    IF HIT(#1, MOUSEX, MOUSEY) <> 4 THEN EXIT SUB
    DrawBird MOUSEX, MOUSEY
    AddBird
  END SUB

  SUB DrawBird(x, y)
    WINDOW USE #1
    BOX x - 3, y - 2, x + 3, y + 2
    LINE x - 8, y - 6, x, y
    LINE x, y, x + 8, y - 6
  END SUB

  SUB AddBird
    count = count + 1
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB Typed
    k$ = KEY$
    IF k$ = "b" THEN DrawBird 40 + count * 20, 100 : AddBird
    IF k$ = "c" THEN Reset
  END SUB

  SUB Reset
    WINDOW USE #1
    PATTERN 0 : BOX 0, 30, 470, 220 : PATTERN 1
    count = 0
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB ShowCount
    WINDOW STATUS #1, STR$(count) + " birds", TIME$
  END SUB

  SUB Tick
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB DoQuit
    END
  END SUB

Type b a few times, click in the sky, type c.

= Step 7: Sound, and asking before quitting
The last step adds sound: SOUND SND_OPEN plays one of the system's sounds
for each bird (silent when the settings say so), and every fifth bird PLAY
plays a tune in the background, on PSG voice 0, while the program goes on.

Birds > Sound switches the sound off and on, with a check mark before the
item (CHECK "Sound", 1). A variable cannot be called sound: SOUND is a
keyword, so it is withsound.

ON QUIT CALL DoQuit makes VeraBASIC Run's own Quit call the program's DoQuit
too, which silences the voices with SOUND OFF before it ends.

That is Bird Watch. Saving the count to a file, a dialog box to ask the
observer's name, an icon for the dock and Make application come with the
Veranda extensions' part 2 (phase 4) and the editor.

  ' Bird Watch, step 7: sound, and asking before quitting
  OPTION INTEGER
  APP NAME "Bird Watch"
  WINDOW #1, 10, 6, 60, 40, "Bird Watch", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW, STATUS 2
  WINDOW USE #1
  FONT UI
  TEXT 16, 20, "Birds at the feeder"
  PAPER 0, 28, 60, 8, GREEN
  PAPER 0, 3, 60, 25, SKY2
  CARDS 40, 1, "Keys: B, C"
  ON KEY CALL Typed
  MENU "Bird Watch" : ITEM "About Bird Watch", About
  MENU "File" : ITEM "Quit", DoQuit, "Q"
  MENU "Birds" : ITEM "Add a bird", AddBird, "B" : ITEM "Start again", Reset
    ITEM "Sound", ToggleSound
  CHECK "Sound", 1
  withsound = 1
  MENU SHOW
  count = 0
  ShowCount
  TIMER 1, 60 CALL Tick
  ON CLICK CALL Clicked
  ON CLOSE #1 CALL DoQuit
  ON QUIT CALL DoQuit
  ON CLOSE #2 CALL CloseAbout

  SUB About
    WINDOW #2, 25, 18, 30, 8, "About", CLOSE, FRAME, SHADOW
    WINDOW USE #2
    FONT UI
    TEXT 12, 20, "Bird Watch 1.0"
    TEXT 12, 36, "Counts the birds at the feeder."
    WINDOW USE #1
  END SUB

  SUB CloseAbout
    WINDOW CLOSE #2
  END SUB

  SUB Clicked
    IF MOUSEB AND 128 THEN EXIT SUB
    IF HIT(#1, MOUSEX, MOUSEY) <> 4 THEN EXIT SUB
    DrawBird MOUSEX, MOUSEY
    AddBird
  END SUB

  SUB DrawBird(x, y)
    WINDOW USE #1
    BOX x - 3, y - 2, x + 3, y + 2
    LINE x - 8, y - 6, x, y
    LINE x, y, x + 8, y - 6
  END SUB

  SUB ToggleSound
    withsound = 1 - withsound
    CHECK "Sound", withsound
  END SUB

  SUB AddBird
    count = count + 1
    IF withsound THEN SOUND SND_OPEN
    IF withsound AND count MOD 5 = 0 THEN PLAY 0, "T200 O5 L16 C E G > C"
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB Typed
    k$ = KEY$
    IF k$ = "b" THEN DrawBird 40 + count * 20, 100 : AddBird
    IF k$ = "c" THEN Reset
  END SUB

  SUB Reset
    WINDOW USE #1
    PATTERN 0 : BOX 0, 30, 470, 220 : PATTERN 1
    count = 0
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB ShowCount
    WINDOW STATUS #1, STR$(count) + " birds", TIME$
  END SUB

  SUB Tick
    ShowCount
  END SUB

  SUB DoQuit
    SOUND OFF
    PRINT "Bird Watch counted"; count; "birds"
    END
  END SUB

Add five birds and listen; switch the sound off with Birds > Sound.

See also: @Contents
